# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.
#
# Responder after RHO overcalls partner's one-level opening with 1NT.
#
# `after-interference.bid` writes every one-level context as `after 1x (1y)`,
# and `1y` binds a suit, so nothing there fires over a notrump overcall and
# responder passed whatever he held. `1D (1N)` and `1C (1N)` were the two
# largest no-rule points in the corpus.
#
# Their 1NT is 15-18 balanced with a stopper, so partner's opening plus our
# own hand locates the rest of the deck: with 10+ total points we own the
# balance and double for penalty. Otherwise it is a competitive auction one
# level up, and the calls are natural. Nine total points is the floor for
# bidding a suit of our own: they have 15-18 and a stopper, so entering at
# the two level on less runs into their strength. BBA declares the bid as
# 7-12 but only makes it from 9 up (366 of the 406 `Opps_Overcall_1NT`
# decisions match at 9; the declared 7 matches 344).
#
# See their-1nt-overcall.notes.md for the BBA meanings this is built from.

module their-1nt-overcall "Responder over their 1NT overcall"
  needs  base

after 1x (1N)
  X   "Penalty: 10+ total points, no long suit of our own"
      shows hcp+length_points>=10
      when  (S<=4 | x is S), (H<=4 | x is H)
      when  C<=5, D<=5
      priority 1

  2{x} "Raise: 6-9 total points, support for partner's suit"
      shows x>=3, tp(x)>=6, tp(x)<=9
      when  x is H | x is S | x>=5
      priority 1                      # a fit first, even holding a suit of our own

  2H  "9+ total points, five or more hearts"
      shows H>=5, hcp+length_points>=9
      when  x is not H

  2S  "9+ total points, five or more spades"
      shows S>=5, hcp+length_points>=9
      when  x is not S

  2C  "9+ total points, six or more clubs"
      shows C>=6, hcp+length_points>=9
      when  x is not C

  2D  "9+ total points, six or more diamonds"
      shows D>=6, hcp+length_points>=9
      when  x is not D

  # Seven cards and too little to bid them at the two level and be
  # raised: jump instead and take the room away. At nine total points
  # both this and the 2-level bid fit, and the seven-card suit says more.
  3C  "Preemptive: seven or more clubs, 5-9 total points"
      shows C>=7, hcp+length_points>=5, hcp+length_points<=9
      when  x is not C
  3D  "Preemptive: seven or more diamonds, 5-9 total points"
      shows D>=7, hcp+length_points>=5, hcp+length_points<=9
      when  x is not D

  # No preemptive jump raise: BBA's 4M over their 1NT is a shapely 11
  # count, not a weak five-card raise, and jumping to game on a raise
  # this side of their 15-18 loses contracts.

  P   "Nothing to say over their notrump"  priority -10
